WEBVTT

00:06.039 --> 00:12.054
[George Santayana]

00:14.422 --> 00:19.500
I've decided that if someone
has to be expelled for this exam…

00:21.516 --> 00:23.226
Yamauchi Haruki.

00:24.406 --> 00:25.590
It should be you.

00:27.676 --> 00:29.238
Why me?!

00:29.496 --> 00:31.073
First of all, all year long…

00:31.308 --> 00:34.535
you've had exceptionally little
contribution to the class.

00:34.560 --> 00:36.576
T-That's not true at all!

00:36.638 --> 00:39.317
Ken and Kanji haven't done much, either!

00:39.982 --> 00:41.231
That's true.

00:42.036 --> 00:46.997
But even compared to them, you still fall short.

00:48.424 --> 00:51.095
What the hell do you think you're saying?!

00:51.291 --> 00:54.181
Aren't you mad? Kanji? Ken?!

00:57.447 --> 01:01.251
H-Hey… Say something already!

01:02.189 --> 01:06.158
Kouenji's the problem here!
He totally blows off the exams!

01:06.183 --> 01:08.110
I've never done anything that bad!

01:08.314 --> 01:11.845
It's true that Kouenji's behavior
could use some improvement.

01:12.377 --> 01:16.126
But in terms of ability, there's a
world of difference between you.

01:17.111 --> 01:19.111
I won't stand for this!

01:19.171 --> 01:20.311
This is just so…

01:24.592 --> 01:26.319
I won't stand for it!

01:26.327 --> 01:30.662
In that case, shall I explain
the decisive point that led me to you?

01:32.585 --> 01:34.490
What decisive point?

01:36.327 --> 01:42.045
You've been fixing the votes to get
Ayanokouji expelled, have you not?

01:43.405 --> 01:45.405
- Huh?
- I can't believe it…

01:50.835 --> 01:54.779
He's trying to get Ayanokouji expelled?

01:57.372 --> 02:00.059
Yes. That is the undeniable truth.

02:00.700 --> 02:02.777
It wasn't me, though!

02:02.825 --> 02:06.752
S-Someone else told me to vote against Ayanokouji!

02:06.872 --> 02:08.378
And who was that?

02:08.434 --> 02:11.832
I, uh… Kanji told me to!

02:11.856 --> 02:12.262
Huh?

02:12.287 --> 02:12.758
Right?

02:12.826 --> 02:14.326
What? I… huh?

02:14.537 --> 02:16.404
Is that true, Ike?

02:16.646 --> 02:19.599
No, it's not! I actually, uh…

02:19.624 --> 02:23.740
I just wanted to help out, because
Kikyou said someone was in danger!

02:24.380 --> 02:27.522
Were you the ringleader, Kushida?

02:27.638 --> 02:31.598
Y-Yeah, that's right! Kikyou dragged me into this!

02:31.630 --> 02:34.098
She said to help get Ayanokouji expelled.

02:34.404 --> 02:35.255
Me?

02:35.326 --> 02:36.849
Isn't that right, everyone?

02:37.045 --> 02:37.771
Hello?!

02:38.068 --> 02:41.388
No… you're so mean, Yamauchi!

02:41.654 --> 02:44.748
Yamauchi begged me to help him,

02:45.256 --> 02:47.373
and I really didn't want to do it,

02:47.670 --> 02:49.935
but I tried so hard to help him anyway!

02:51.506 --> 02:52.529
Kushida.

02:53.178 --> 02:55.880
You're highly influential in this class.

02:56.842 --> 03:00.373
I'm sure you knew what would happen
if you agreed to help him.

03:01.412 --> 03:04.982
I'd ask you to act in the class's
best interest going forward.

03:06.246 --> 03:07.312
That said,

03:07.559 --> 03:11.066
it doesn't change the fact
that Yamauchi started this.

03:11.246 --> 03:13.895
- Hold on, Horikita! I'm telling you, I didn't…

03:13.895 --> 03:15.043
- My, my…
- Hold on, Horikita! I'm telling you, I didn't…

03:15.070 --> 03:17.572
This goes deeper than I thought.

03:17.862 --> 03:24.830
But there's nothing untoward in trying to
get rid of someone in this particular exam.

03:25.309 --> 03:30.183
Do you have some reason for being
so harsh to him in particular?

03:30.356 --> 03:31.777
Y-Yeah!

03:31.942 --> 03:33.019
Yamauchi.

03:33.715 --> 03:38.754
You've been working with Sakayanagi behind
our backs, and acting on her orders, correct?

03:39.012 --> 03:40.308
- What?!
- Hey, Haruki!

03:40.333 --> 03:41.902
What is she talking about?

03:41.942 --> 03:44.910
That's ridiculous! Where's your proof, huh?!

03:45.239 --> 03:47.573
Perhaps you'll show us your phone.

03:48.283 --> 03:51.345
I'm sure Sakayanagi is saved in your contacts.

03:51.572 --> 03:52.627
That's 'cause…

03:53.057 --> 03:56.619
…we're friends, okay?
There's nothing wrong with that!

03:56.653 --> 03:59.572
Wait, you're seriously cozying up to Class A?!

03:59.674 --> 04:02.369
N-Not so much that I'd sell out my friends!

04:03.486 --> 04:04.674
Don't be silly.

04:05.384 --> 04:09.384
Maybe she made you an offer you couldn't refuse.

04:09.783 --> 04:13.571
For instance, offering to date you.

04:14.884 --> 04:16.212
He's going out with her?

04:16.283 --> 04:17.814
What a scumbag.

04:18.119 --> 04:23.486
I can't allow a student more capable than you
to be expelled over something so trivial.

04:23.783 --> 04:27.915
This makes you the best candidate for expulsion.

04:28.408 --> 04:31.978
Colluding with the enemy against
a classmate, without a thought.

04:32.119 --> 04:35.384
If you'd single out one of your own like that,

04:35.954 --> 04:40.586
you are the one this class does not need.

04:40.774 --> 04:42.148
That's not…

04:42.243 --> 04:43.883
No objections, then.

04:44.164 --> 04:47.961
Horikita, my girl, I suppose
I'll follow your lead.

04:48.071 --> 04:52.351
H-Hang on a sec! I'm not a traitor,
I swear on my life!

04:52.383 --> 04:54.570
If anyone is opposed to what I've said,

04:54.758 --> 04:57.156
you're free to vote against me.

04:57.594 --> 04:59.851
I've said my piece.

05:00.352 --> 05:03.512
Take that as you will, and vote carefully.

05:04.086 --> 05:07.430
Wait, Suzune! I get what you're saying.

05:07.688 --> 05:09.937
But I can't go along with this.

05:10.336 --> 05:12.461
I can't get a friend kicked out!

05:12.852 --> 05:15.937
I appreciate how important friendship is to you.

05:16.813 --> 05:21.195
But in protecting one person, you'll only
end up turning your back on another.

05:22.219 --> 05:24.533
We cannot let emotions dictate this exam.

05:24.868 --> 05:27.148
We must proceed based on logic.

05:28.547 --> 05:30.062
Sorry, Haruki.

05:30.282 --> 05:32.383
There's nothing I can do.

05:32.422 --> 05:33.226
Huh?!

05:33.625 --> 05:35.195
That settles it.

05:35.258 --> 05:37.578
Wait, wait, just wait a minute!

05:37.610 --> 05:39.195
This is just ridiculous!

05:39.258 --> 05:43.750
Say what you will, but no one deserves
negative votes more than you do.

05:44.032 --> 05:45.992
Think whatever you want!

05:46.024 --> 05:48.062
But everyone else already promised!

05:48.352 --> 05:50.263
They're gonna vote Ayanokouji out.

05:50.288 --> 05:53.187
You won't go back on your
promise to Kikyou, right?!

05:53.708 --> 05:55.247
I take it back.

05:55.272 --> 05:55.880
Huh?

05:55.950 --> 05:57.708
I had it all wrong.

05:58.013 --> 06:02.302
I asked you all to vote with me,
but I take it back!

06:02.552 --> 06:04.512
Hold it, Kushida!

06:04.638 --> 06:06.512
Taking it back now is just low!

06:06.661 --> 06:08.661
You're the one who's low, Yamauchi!

06:08.740 --> 06:11.458
How could you betray your class like this?

06:11.919 --> 06:12.706
You bitch!

06:19.404 --> 06:22.770
You are the weakest link in this class.

06:22.927 --> 06:25.778
Moreover, you are a traitor.

06:25.958 --> 06:27.872
That's reason enough for me.

06:27.958 --> 06:29.872
Wait a moment, Horikita!

06:31.005 --> 06:32.614
What is it, Hirata?

06:33.068 --> 06:35.606
I let you say what you needed to say, but…

06:36.333 --> 06:38.653
this isn't the way to do this!

06:38.833 --> 06:40.239
Thank god…

06:40.286 --> 06:42.911
We can't have this in-fighting, it's not right!

06:43.294 --> 06:45.294
There is no way around it.

06:45.508 --> 06:48.047
You still haven't accepted that?

06:48.187 --> 06:50.375
How could I accept something like that?

06:50.579 --> 06:52.703
I don't want to lose any of you!

06:52.875 --> 06:54.703
Y-Yeah, he's right!

06:54.750 --> 06:59.117
Say what you will, but I'll fight as I see fit.

06:59.796 --> 07:04.272
Let's take a poll now on whether or not
to vote against Yamauchi.

07:04.461 --> 07:05.675
You can't do that!

07:05.829 --> 07:07.344
I'll begin now.

07:07.540 --> 07:10.180
I'm asking you to stop, Horikita.

07:10.594 --> 07:12.527
You have no right to stop me.

07:12.863 --> 07:15.433
What you're saying isn't right.

07:15.551 --> 07:17.660
What would you say is right, then?

07:17.785 --> 07:18.714
I am…

07:19.535 --> 07:21.058
Horikita.

07:21.402 --> 07:23.109
Shut up for a second.

07:24.199 --> 07:26.058
Hirata…?

07:26.083 --> 07:27.864
Alright, everybody, listen up!

07:30.363 --> 07:33.652
I don't know if all of this is true,
but it doesn't matter.

07:33.691 --> 07:37.371
It isn't true, Hirata! I'm being framed!

07:37.771 --> 07:39.232
Framed?

07:39.935 --> 07:43.966
After all of this, can you really
say you weren't involved?

07:44.904 --> 07:46.388
But he's not the only one.

07:46.669 --> 07:50.888
You're all so quick to throw a classmate
under the bus, it makes me sick.

07:51.193 --> 07:55.141
The exam is tomorrow.
You want to go into it with no plan?

07:55.381 --> 07:57.443
What's wrong with not having a plan?

07:58.123 --> 08:01.052
What right do we have to judge our classmates?

08:01.326 --> 08:02.693
What are you saying?

08:02.935 --> 08:05.630
Maybe you're the one who doesn't belong here.

08:06.451 --> 08:11.279
Stringing everyone along to bring
someone else down isn't right.

08:11.779 --> 08:12.966
How idealistic.

08:13.162 --> 08:17.536
He already formed a group right under
your nose to bring Ayanokouji down.

08:17.740 --> 08:21.161
Yes. That's despicable as well.

08:21.568 --> 08:25.544
But the way you're inciting
everyone now is on another level!

08:26.052 --> 08:28.634
No, it's not. It's exactly the same.

08:29.073 --> 08:33.596
Even if we don't hold a poll now,
I've already explained my reasoning.

08:33.979 --> 08:35.448
You're right.

08:35.807 --> 08:38.010
The die has been cast.

08:39.621 --> 08:40.437
In that case,

08:40.871 --> 08:45.785
I'll be issuing a negative vote
against you tomorrow.

08:46.223 --> 08:48.635
I won't go along with this.

08:48.831 --> 08:50.643
Yes, do as you please.

08:50.745 --> 08:54.432
I'm sure this exam seems unfair to you.

08:54.737 --> 09:00.463
But make no mistake. In the real world, you'll all
face situations where someone has to go.

09:00.901 --> 09:05.455
Those in positions of power will have
no choice but to bring down the hammer.

09:06.198 --> 09:10.901
Moreover, if you see this exam as
a mere hindrance, you'll learn nothing.

09:11.636 --> 09:16.026
I won't insert myself into this discussion.

09:16.737 --> 09:21.416
All you can do is think carefully
about your votes tomorrow.

09:30.916 --> 09:34.174
After tomorrow, I never have to
see Ryuuen's face again!

09:34.666 --> 09:36.174
Smooth sailing from now on.

09:36.346 --> 09:37.986
Someone doesn't look happy.

09:38.119 --> 09:40.994
Do you want Ryuuen to stay that badly?

09:43.416 --> 09:45.837
Do you need to bother me that badly?

09:46.158 --> 09:47.298
Not really.

09:47.650 --> 09:51.548
Hey, I know I'm voting against you,

09:52.064 --> 09:54.915
but are you voting against me, too, Ibuki?

09:55.119 --> 09:56.150
Who knows.

09:56.549 --> 09:57.634
Fine, then.

09:58.314 --> 10:00.251
Play it cool if you want,

10:00.463 --> 10:03.345
but once Ryuuen's expelled, you're next.

10:05.103 --> 10:06.712
Ibuki. Got a minute?

10:07.080 --> 10:08.290
What do you want?

10:08.385 --> 10:11.237
It's about Ryuuen's private points.

10:11.385 --> 10:12.407
How'd it go?

10:12.603 --> 10:14.290
Nothing to report.

10:14.424 --> 10:16.407
You still haven't transferred them?

10:16.799 --> 10:19.618
When he gets expelled, we'll lose them all!

10:19.885 --> 10:23.181
Okay, why don't you go beg for them, then?

10:23.713 --> 10:25.454
I can't do anything.

10:26.056 --> 10:30.337
Well, I guess you do come off as
his underling who went rogue.

10:30.869 --> 10:33.462
If anyone saw you with him, it'd look sketchy.

10:33.588 --> 10:36.470
Damn, what am I even doing?

10:37.072 --> 10:41.236
Isn't it best for you if Ryuuen
gets expelled, anyway?

10:42.119 --> 10:44.119
Is that okay with you?

10:44.181 --> 10:47.814
Without him, we can kiss any hope of
getting to Class A goodbye!

10:53.478 --> 10:55.665
The point transfer went though.

10:55.767 --> 10:57.548
You've finished your duties now.

10:59.002 --> 11:01.087
How bold of you.

11:01.525 --> 11:03.181
Isn't this what you wanted?

11:03.392 --> 11:06.634
If you didn't want to,
you could have just spent them.

11:09.353 --> 11:12.462
Wh… What the hell are you doing?!

11:16.517 --> 11:20.259
You're a feisty one. I like that about you.

11:20.306 --> 11:21.353
What?!

11:23.931 --> 11:26.837
You're tough, but you have too many weak spots.

11:27.213 --> 11:29.642
You'll never beat Suzune like that.

11:30.064 --> 11:31.540
Mind your own business.

11:31.642 --> 11:32.861
See you around.

11:36.572 --> 11:39.884
Hey, did you like being at this school?

11:39.924 --> 11:40.798
Huh?

11:42.767 --> 11:44.087
Forget it.

11:55.299 --> 11:57.806
I got Ryuuen's private points.

11:58.593 --> 12:00.595
[Student Council President
Nagumo Miyabi]

12:05.197 --> 12:10.204
Don't worry, everyone!
No one here is getting expelled.

12:10.596 --> 12:14.540
But how are you going to get
the rest of the points we need?

12:14.931 --> 12:19.142
President Nagumo agreed to
lend us the rest of the points!

12:19.330 --> 12:20.736
President Nagumo did?

12:21.064 --> 12:24.845
Things will be pretty tight until I can
get everyone reimbursed, but…

12:25.033 --> 12:26.665
do we still want to do this?

12:27.033 --> 12:29.759
Yes! You're the best, Honami!

12:29.791 --> 12:31.923
Of course, we're all in!

12:43.142 --> 12:46.017
Honami. I assume I know why you're calling.

12:46.556 --> 12:47.642
Yes.

12:48.142 --> 12:51.814
There's just one thing I wanted to check with you.

12:52.041 --> 12:53.126
What is it?

12:53.291 --> 12:56.868
It's just, well… I mean…

12:58.017 --> 13:01.439
D-Do you… actually like me?

13:01.783 --> 13:04.704
I'd hardly be doing this if I didn't like you.

13:05.846 --> 13:08.690
If you've made up your mind, I'll send the points.

13:08.806 --> 13:10.806
We can consider the contract signed.

13:10.931 --> 13:12.197
Wait a moment.

13:12.705 --> 13:15.545
I'd like to try on my own until the last moment.

13:16.119 --> 13:20.236
Careful, now. The offer expires at midnight.

13:20.431 --> 13:23.243
I keep a tight schedule, you see.

13:23.681 --> 13:26.314
Yes. You'll hear from me before then.

13:33.697 --> 13:36.079
I really thought I was ready, too.

13:43.471 --> 13:45.987
And how is Katsuragi doing?

13:47.049 --> 13:49.142
Pretty tight-lipped.

13:49.328 --> 13:52.111
Seems like he's come to terms with being expelled.

13:53.775 --> 13:55.478
That's wonderful to hear.

13:55.705 --> 14:01.837
By the way, it seems my collaboration
with Yamauchi has been exposed.

14:02.056 --> 14:04.337
Sounds like you slipped up, Sakayanagi.

14:04.626 --> 14:08.141
I knew the class would end up holding a trial.

14:08.369 --> 14:10.533
It was only a matter of time.

14:10.775 --> 14:14.689
But now it's not clear who
they'll have expelled anymore.

14:15.072 --> 14:18.243
No, it's clear as can be.

14:18.759 --> 14:23.313
Yes, you really should leave the king
on the board until the very end.

14:30.869 --> 14:34.173
[Additional Special Exam
Start Time: 9:00am]

14:34.174 --> 14:35.875
Without any further ado,

14:35.939 --> 14:37.877
let's begin the class voting.

14:40.004 --> 14:45.009
[Classroom of the Elite
3rd Season]

14:45.034 --> 14:47.142
[Additional Special Exam
Results to be Announced]

14:47.150 --> 14:49.497
[Additional Special Exam
Results to be Announced]
You gotta be quiet, Haruki!

14:49.497 --> 14:50.040
You gotta be quiet, Haruki!

14:50.221 --> 14:51.197
Shut up!

14:52.963 --> 14:56.501
Trembling as you await your fate, I see.

14:58.431 --> 15:01.001
I guess there's no harm in telling you now.

15:01.025 --> 15:05.404
Sorry to disappoint you!
I'm not the one getting expelled!

15:05.502 --> 15:06.493
Oh?

15:06.760 --> 15:12.111
See, Sakayanagi is giving me
Class A's positive votes!

15:12.228 --> 15:15.623
So no matter how many of you
voted against me, it's no use!

15:16.705 --> 15:20.197
You hear me? I've got Class A protecting me!

15:23.596 --> 15:26.572
So, how many of you voted against me?

15:27.322 --> 15:30.611
I didn't even betray you in the first place.

15:30.705 --> 15:32.619
And this is how you treat me?

15:33.486 --> 15:36.517
But no hard feelings! I forgive you.

15:39.909 --> 15:41.878
Take your seat, Yamauchi.

15:41.925 --> 15:43.417
Roger.

15:44.300 --> 15:46.198
I'll announce the results now.

15:48.441 --> 15:51.745
I'll start with third place for positive votes.

15:52.519 --> 15:53.721
Which is…

15:54.284 --> 15:55.550
Kushida Kikyou.

15:56.472 --> 15:58.057
Moving on to second place…

15:59.417 --> 16:00.846
Hirata Yousuke.

16:00.941 --> 16:03.572
- Hirata's in second?
- See, he can do no wrong.

16:03.691 --> 16:06.886
His reputation didn't take much
of a hit after yesterday.

16:07.816 --> 16:12.745
Hirata's built up enough trust over
the past year to override that.

16:13.636 --> 16:17.487
B-But wait, if Hirata's number two,
who's above him?

16:17.643 --> 16:20.003
In first place with the most positive votes…

16:26.620 --> 16:28.446
Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.

16:29.183 --> 16:30.198
That would be you.

16:30.223 --> 16:32.542
- Ayanokouji? Why him?
- I didn't see that coming…

16:32.769 --> 16:34.878
Huh? Ayanokouji?!

16:34.952 --> 16:37.620
Don't you have first place wrong?

16:37.941 --> 16:39.472
No, this is correct.

16:40.152 --> 16:41.690
What have you been up to?

16:42.144 --> 16:44.612
In last place,
with the most negative votes…

16:44.706 --> 16:46.340
Unfortunately, that'd be you.

16:46.652 --> 16:48.011
Yamauchi Haruki.

16:48.128 --> 16:49.058
How?

16:49.355 --> 16:51.840
How, how, how could this happen?!

16:53.246 --> 16:54.909
This can't be…

16:55.316 --> 16:57.316
This exam is a joke!

16:57.472 --> 17:00.690
You're entitled to your opinion,
but the result remains.

17:00.707 --> 17:01.925
Shut it!

17:02.253 --> 17:07.519
Oh, right, all you have to do is ask Sakayanagi!
She promised me those votes!

17:07.884 --> 17:10.109
Is she allowed to just lie about it?!

17:10.767 --> 17:12.767
You're dismissed, Yamauchi.

17:13.376 --> 17:14.204
No…

17:14.470 --> 17:16.056
No, this can't be happening!

17:16.361 --> 17:18.517
Hurry and take your leave, now.

17:18.736 --> 17:21.617
You've already been deleted.

17:21.689 --> 17:23.689
I'm not letting this happen!

17:24.025 --> 17:27.454
So you're determined to be miserable,
unseemly, and hopeless

17:27.806 --> 17:31.110
right until the bitter end, are you?

17:36.472 --> 17:38.776
You were ready to do me in.

17:39.159 --> 17:42.060
So I don't want to hear
any complaints from you now.

17:43.815 --> 17:45.237
That's quite enough.

17:46.081 --> 17:48.463
Don't push this any further, Yamauchi.

17:48.761 --> 17:49.940
For your own sake.

18:16.666 --> 18:18.100
The lowest voted student…

18:19.798 --> 18:21.001
Totsuka Yahiko.

18:24.071 --> 18:25.093
That's ridiculous!

18:25.875 --> 18:29.734
Sakayanagi! I thought you
fixed the vote against me!

18:31.522 --> 18:33.443
The answer is simple.

18:33.647 --> 18:36.576
You are more capable than Totsuka.

18:36.967 --> 18:39.990
I can't let go of one of my best pawns.

18:40.741 --> 18:42.100
Damn it!

18:42.866 --> 18:46.248
Now, I wonder how the other classes

18:46.430 --> 18:48.133
are faring right about now?

18:52.757 --> 18:55.260
[Expelled:
Class A, Totsuka Yakiko; Class B, N/A;
Class C, Yamauchi Haruki; Class D, Manabe Shiho]

18:57.760 --> 18:59.510
[Manabe Shiho]

18:59.526 --> 19:01.190
That Manabe…

19:01.284 --> 19:03.151
She sure can scream.

19:03.190 --> 19:04.140
Oh, really.

19:08.120 --> 19:09.729
Hey, Ayanokouji.

19:10.230 --> 19:12.784
Since when are you such a nice guy?

19:13.159 --> 19:14.393
What do you mean?

19:14.433 --> 19:15.799
Don't play dumb.

19:16.448 --> 19:19.213
Why did you bother to save me?

19:19.644 --> 19:23.424
It was those dear friends of you who bothered.

19:24.040 --> 19:25.682
[A Few Days Ago]

19:25.698 --> 19:27.206
[A Few Days Ago]
I'm begging you, Ayanokouji!

19:27.753 --> 19:30.956
Tell me how to keep Ryuuen from getting expelled!

19:31.222 --> 19:33.698
I can't make that happen.

19:34.198 --> 19:36.487
You must be able to do something!

19:36.901 --> 19:38.995
He's already made peace with it.

19:39.355 --> 19:43.401
Anyone who cares about him
should sympathize with that.

19:43.456 --> 19:45.495
I know, but I…

19:46.433 --> 19:49.151
The only advice I can give you

19:49.409 --> 19:51.570
is about Ryuuen's private points.

19:51.807 --> 19:54.268
It would be a shame for them to go to waste.

19:54.398 --> 19:58.070
What's your problem?! What, so we
take his points and wave goodbye?

19:58.245 --> 20:04.730
This exam isn't so easy that you can
save someone just by saying you want to.

20:05.503 --> 20:07.690
Are you prepared for that?

20:07.901 --> 20:08.963
Prepared?

20:16.573 --> 20:19.159
I got Ryuuen's private points.

20:19.956 --> 20:21.956
How many did he have?

20:22.011 --> 20:23.338
Around five million.

20:23.581 --> 20:24.823
That's plenty.

20:25.433 --> 20:27.479
I'm going to make a call.

20:28.597 --> 20:30.597
Meet me back at my room.

20:32.495 --> 20:33.393
Are you serious?

20:35.097 --> 20:36.206
Good evening!

20:37.206 --> 20:38.706
G-Good evening.

20:41.394 --> 20:46.746
I'll talk to everyone in Class B and have them
give Ryuuen their positive votes.

20:46.973 --> 20:51.380
In return, I'll just ask you
for the points we still need.

20:51.950 --> 20:54.770
This way, no one in Class B gets expelled,

20:55.059 --> 20:57.551
and Ryuuen can stay in Class D.

20:57.762 --> 20:59.809
Sounds like a win-win to me.

20:59.848 --> 21:01.317
I-I get it now.

21:01.333 --> 21:03.277
But you're not too smart, are you?

21:03.520 --> 21:04.100
Huh?

21:04.426 --> 21:08.317
You worked hard for those points,
and you're just giving them all up.

21:08.833 --> 21:12.285
I don't think you have any room
to speak on that, Ibuki.

21:12.512 --> 21:13.168
Huh?

21:13.270 --> 21:17.199
You managed to get your hands
on five million points,

21:17.309 --> 21:19.645
and you're using them to save Ryuuen.

21:20.739 --> 21:22.490
That's a different story.

21:23.012 --> 21:27.074
Besides, this is bad news for whoever
gets kicked out instead of Ryuuen.

21:28.817 --> 21:30.551
That might even be me.

21:30.919 --> 21:34.457
But you've chosen to save Ryuuen, all the same.

21:35.120 --> 21:40.299
I just don't want him to get any
weird ideas about me owing him.

21:48.442 --> 21:51.871
You're saying Ishizaki and Ibuki saved me?

21:52.340 --> 21:54.676
Now that's what I call misplaced kindness.

21:54.779 --> 21:56.232
What's your plan now?

21:56.678 --> 21:58.036
We'll see.

22:04.780 --> 22:06.280
[New Message
From: Sakayanagi Arisu]
